{"abstract":[{"text":"Follow a request from the socket to your handler and back.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/HowARequestIsServed"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NanoHTTP"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"How a Request Is Served"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"code":["start()  ──►  listening socket  ──►  accept loop (a thread of its own)","                                           │ accepts a connection (over maxConnections ──► 503)","                                           ▼","                              a thread of its own serves the connection:","                                           │","        ┌──────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐","        ▼                                                                  │","   wait for the request (idleTimeout), NanoHTTPParser reads it             │","        │   Expect: 100-continue ──► 100 Continue                          │","        │   chunked bodies are put together                                │","        │   too large or malformed ──► 400 / 413 / 414 / 417 / 431 / 501 / 505,","        │   connection closed; stalls (readTimeout) ──► 408, connection closed","        ▼                                                                  │","   dispatch(request:)                                                      │","        │   middleware, outermost first, each around the rest              │","        │   router: method + path ──► handler and route variables          │","        │   HEAD ──► the GET handler; other methods of the path ──► 405    │","        │   OPTIONS answered; no route ──► notFoundHandler, else 404       │","        ▼                                                                  │","   the handler returns a NanoHTTPResponse (or throws: NanoHTTPError)       │","        ▼                                                                  │","   the response is written: head and body in one piece, or the body        │","        in chunks, or with the length that the handler declared            │","        │   a socket session (WebSocket) runs now, then the connection ends│","        ▼                                                                  │","   does the client want to keep the connection, and is the end of the      │","   response known? (HTTP/1.1: yes, unless it said Connection: close) ──────┘","        │ no","        ▼","   Connection: close was sent, and the connection is closed"],"syntax":"text","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" creates the listening socket (at the address of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and starts the accept loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/listen()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Failures to accept do not end the loop, unless the listening socket is gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each accepted connection is registered with the server, so that ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/stop()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" can close it, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted: when ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/maxConnections","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" connections are open, the new one is answered with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"503","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and closed. Otherwise a thread of its own serves the connection.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The thread waits for the first byte of a request for at most the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/idleTimeout","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a silent connection is closed). A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" then reads the request. It reads exactly as much as its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" allow, and waits at most the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/readTimeout","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Requests that exceed a limit, are malformed or stall are answered by the server with ","type":"text"},{"code":"400","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"408","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"413","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"414","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"431","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the connection is closed after the answer, once the client has had the chance to read it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" finds the handler. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs the middleware, then the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"router, then the ","type":"text"},{"code":"notFoundHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The handler returns a response; the response is written. A body that cannot be produced (invalid JSON) becomes a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"500","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the client wants to keep the connection (HTTP/1.1: unless it said ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connection: close","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and the end of the response is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"known, the thread waits for the next request on it; otherwise the connection is closed. A WebSocket response keeps the thread: the session runs until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the connection ends.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" there are no threads for connections: the accepting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thread waits for the listening socket and all connections together, serves the connection that has data (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request, then back to waiting), drives the sessions of WebSockets, and closes the connections that stay silent for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the idle timeout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A subclass that hands its requests to other threads can answer later: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection/deferResponse()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the connection waits for its answer without being read or timed out, and the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the answer on a thread of its own when it is sent, in both threading modes (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/stop()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" closes the listening socket and all registered connections: threads that wait for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a request return, and threads that are writing fail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The types involved: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (sockets and threads), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (routing),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (one request with its handler), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (reading), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoSocket","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connection), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The file ","type":"text"},{"code":"ARCHITECTURE.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the repository describes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same machinery for people who change it: layers, locks, and why things are the way they are.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP":{"abstract":[{"text":"A small HTTP/1.1 server for apps and tools: routing, files, forms, uploads and WebSockets, without dependencies.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"NanoHTTP","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Logging":{"abstract":[{"text":"See what the server reports, and send it where you want it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Logging","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Logging","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/logging"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending":{"abstract":[{"text":"Look at every request before it is routed, and replace parts of the server by subclassing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Middleware and Extending the Server","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/middlewareandextending"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"A logger that prints one line for every message, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[WARNING] Unable to accept a connection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for command-line tools and for tests. By default the lines are printed to the standard output, and every line is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flushed: when the output goes to a pipe or a file (","type":"text"},{"code":"tool | tee log","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), the standard output is buffered, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lines would otherwise show up late.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoConsoleLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanoconsolelogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection":{"abstract":[{"text":"A request that has been read from a connection, together with the handler that will answer it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drives the connection with it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"send(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response and returns the connection for the next request, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the connection has ended.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPConnection","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpconnection"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection/deferResponse()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Promises to answer the request later, from any thread, with the returned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Call it in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(and nowhere else), before it returns; the connection is not answered when ","type":"text"},{"code":"handle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns. Calling it again for the same request returns the same token.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deferResponse"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A20HTTPDeferredResponseC","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection/deferResponse()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"deferResponse()","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpconnection/deferresponse()"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse":{"abstract":[{"text":"The answer to a request that is sent later, from any thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpdeferredresponse"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives the messages that a server reports: a response that could not be written, a pause in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepting connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that broke the protocol.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Set the logger of a server with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttplogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"Reads HTTP requests from a socket.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPParser"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpparser"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"Upper bounds for the size of a request.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Limits"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Limits"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPParser.Limits","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpparser/limits-swift.struct"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest":{"abstract":[{"text":"An HTTP request: method, path, query, headers and body, plus the address of the client and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"variables of the route that matched. The server creates one for every request and hands it to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"middleware and handlers. A request is a reference type, compared and hashed by identity.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPRequest"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPRequest"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPRequest","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttprequest"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse":{"abstract":[{"text":"The answer to a request: a status code, headers and a body. Use the static functions to create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the common responses:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPResponse","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpresponse"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer":{"abstract":[{"text":"An HTTP/1.1 server with routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServer","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserver"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO":{"abstract":[{"text":"The part of a server that deals with sockets and threads: it listens at a port, accepts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections, reads the requests of each connection on a thread of its own, hands them to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and writes the responses. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" builds routing on top of it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subclass this class to use the server without routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread":{"abstract":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One thread does everything","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it accepts connections, reads requests, calls the middleware","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the handlers, and writes the responses, one request at a time. Handlers, middleware and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"everything else that runs in them need no locks, because they never run at the same time.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" starts that thread (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is its priority);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses the calling thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"singleThread"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO.Configuration.Threading.singleThread","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/threading-swift.enum/singlethread"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS":{"abstract":[{"text":"The priority of the thread that accepts connections.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"acceptQoS"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@E@NSQualityOfService","text":"QualityOfService"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"acceptQoS","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/acceptqos"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/idleTimeout":{"abstract":[{"text":"How long a connection may wait for a request to begin: after it was accepted, and after a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response when the connection is kept alive. A connection that stays silent that long is closed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without an answer. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or zero) waits forever. The default is 60 seconds.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"idleTimeout"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","text":"TimeInterval"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/idleTimeout","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"idleTimeout","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/idletimeout"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where the server listens. The default is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/NanoListenAddress/loopback","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": only programs on this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"machine can connect. Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/NanoListenAddress/allInterfaces","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a server that is meant to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be reached from other devices.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"listenAddress"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A12HTTPServerIOC0A13ListenAddressO","text":"NanoListenAddress"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"listenAddress","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/listenaddress"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives what the server reports: a response that could not be written, a pause in accepting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that broke the protocol. The default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoOSLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which writes to the unified logging system (the console of Xcode, the Console","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app). A command-line tool that should print to its terminal uses a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoSilentLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" switches logging off.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"logger"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A10HTTPLoggerP","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"logger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/logger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/maxConnections":{"abstract":[{"text":"The most connections the server serves at the same time (WebSocket sessions included). When","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that many are open, a new connection is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"503 Service Unavailable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and closed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts any number; every connection uses a thread and a file descriptor. The default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is 128.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maxConnections"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/maxConnections","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"maxConnections","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/maxconnections"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/readTimeout":{"abstract":[{"text":"How long the server waits for more of a request once it has begun: the longest pause between two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parts of the request that arrive. A request that stalls longer is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"408 Request Timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It is a pause, not the total time: a request that keeps arriving, slowly, is not cut","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"off. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or zero) waits forever. The default is 30 seconds.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"readTimeout"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","text":"TimeInterval"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/readTimeout","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"readTimeout","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/readtimeout"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/threading-swift.property":{"abstract":[{"text":"Which threads run the server, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The default is ","type":"text"}